---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import SectionMarker from "../components/SectionMarker.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { links } from "../data/site";

const updated = "31 October 2026";
---

<Base title="Privacy — klaus." description="Privacy notice for klyse.eu.">
  <Nav sections={false} />
  <main>
    <section class="section wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <SectionMarker number="§" label="Privacy" />
        <h1 class="t-title">Privacy notice</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          klyse.eu is my private, non-commercial website. This notice explains how personal data is handled when you
          visit it.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Who is responsible</h2>
        <p>
          Email: <a href={`mailto:${links.email}`}>{links.email}</a>
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Hosting</h2>
        <p>
          The site is hosted by Vercel Inc., 440 N Barranca Ave #4133, Covina, CA 91723, USA. To deliver pages and keep
          the site secure, technical data such as your IP address, the time of your visit, the page requested and your
          browser details may be processed and logged. This is based on my legitimate interest in running a working,
          secure website (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). The data is kept only as long as needed for these purposes.
        </p>
        <p>
          Vercel may process data outside the EU, including in the USA. Where that happens, it is covered by the
          safeguards the GDPR provides for, such as adequacy decisions or standard contractual clauses.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Visitor statistics</h2>
        <p>
          To see how many people visit the site and which pages they read, I use Vercel Web Analytics. It counts page
          views together with the page address, the referring site, and your country, browser, operating system and
          device type. It sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser. Visitors are told apart only by a hash
          of the request that is reset every day, so you cannot be recognised across days or other websites, and I
          cannot identify you.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is based on my legitimate interest in understanding how the site is used (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). You can
          object at any time, for example by blocking scripts from this site or writing to me. More information is in
          <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Vercel's
          analytics privacy notes</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Settings in your browser</h2>
        <p>
          The site may store small settings in your browser, such as your choice of light or dark theme, so it can
          remember them. You can delete them at any time in your browser settings.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>The site links to other websites. Their own privacy policies apply once you follow a link.</p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under the GDPR you have the right to access, correct and delete your data, to restrict or object to its
          processing, and to data portability. Just write to me at the address above. You can also lodge a complaint with
          a supervisory authority, in Italy the Garante per la protezione dei dati personali.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Changes</h2>
        <p>I may update this notice when the site changes. The current version is always on this page.</p>

        <p class="t-meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .section-head h1 { margin: 0; }
  .prose { max-width: 68ch; }
  .prose p { margin: 0 0 var(--step-4); }
  .prose h2 { margin: var(--step-12) 0 var(--step-4); }
  .t-meta { margin-top: var(--step-12); color: var(--ink-muted); }
</style>
